  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "AFB-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "One arithmetic unit separates all positive translation degrees in range",
      "anchor": "inputs-affine-block",
      "statement": "For a totally complex number field and 1≤m<r₂ there exists one unit v whose absolute place products of every total degree from 1 to m differ from one. In each such degree j the action of multiplication by v on the real cohomology of the additive n-by-r matrix lattice is annihilated by a real polynomial F_j with F_j(1)≠0.",
      "hypotheses": "At complex places use the ordinary complex modulus, one place per conjugate pair. The exponent vectors are nonnegative integral. The additive group of rectangular matrices over the ring of integers is a finite-rank free abelian group. The block sizes n,r do not enter the strict bound m<r₂.",
      "definitions": [
        "A=Mat_{n×r}(𝒪_L′) with addition",
        "The kernel of the logarithmic character for a given exponent vector is a subgroup of infinite index. Several exponent vectors can define the same kernel.",
        "real factor (X−Λ)(X−conj(Λ)) for each j-fold product of embedding eigenvalues",
        "a unit u=v⁻¹I_n gives s(u)⁻¹x s(u) acting by v on A"
      ],
