      "anchor": "inputs-affine-cycle-proof",
      "statement": "Let f:H→GL_{n+r}(𝒪_L′) be block upper triangular with corner maps f₀:H→GL_n(𝒪_L′) and I_r. On any real m-cycle, f and diag(f₀,I_r) differ by a boundary in GL_{n+r}(𝒪_L′) for 1≤m<r₂. This removes the off-diagonal block in the Hecke computation on a complementary coset stabilizer.",
      "hypotheses": "L′ is fixed and totally complex with r₂ complex places. H is any group for the affine theorem. The attached Hecke computation assumes positive n,r and its separate integral block factorization, arithmetic-invariant closed cochain and basepoint-independence result. The larger stable-homology theorem uses its own stabilization range.",
