      "review": "For L′=ℚ(i,√5) one has r₂=2. With v=(1+√5)/2, conjugation of U(v) by diag(v,1) gives U(v²). Multiplication by U(−v) produces U(1), hence the affine generator U(1)diag(v,1) agrees with diag(v,1) in abelianization.",
      "correspondence": "The split-group double complex passes the annihilating polynomial from the additive kernel to positive vertical degrees. The prism comparison with right translation evaluates it at 1. Separation by real cocycles turns the resulting pullback identity into a bounding chain, which maps into GL of size n+r and is used on the Hecke stabilizer."
